WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.623
In this lesson, you will learn to make
Layouts that fit the way you work.

00:00:05.973 --> 00:00:09.720
The best Layout depends on two things: the
shape of your display,

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.988
and what you do on it.

00:00:10.988 --> 00:00:13.121
A few minutes here pay off every day.

00:00:14.487 --> 00:00:18.238
Click the Zonal icon in the menu bar, and
choose Edit Layouts.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:22.573
The Layouts window opens. Your Layouts are
listed on the left.

00:00:22.573 --> 00:00:27.199
Select one to change its name, its
spacing, or the display that uses it.

00:00:27.703 --> 00:00:32.490
To change the Zones themselves, click Edit
on, followed by the name of your display.

00:00:32.938 --> 00:00:35.048
The editor covers the whole display,

00:00:35.048 --> 00:00:38.974
so you work at real size and see exactly
how big each Zone will be.

00:00:39.443 --> 00:00:41.559
Click a Zone to split it in two.

00:00:41.559 --> 00:00:46.452
A wide Zone becomes two Zones side by
side, a tall Zone two stacked Zones.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.302
Hold Shift while you click to split the
other way.

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:53.157
Drag the divider between two Zones to
resize them both.

00:00:53.157 --> 00:00:56.901
It moves in steps of five percent, so your
Zones stay tidy.

00:00:57.331 --> 00:01:01.220
To join Zones, Command-click each of them,
then click Merge.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:04.785
Together, they must form a rectangle, or
Zonal refuses.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:09.739
Made a mistake? Undo takes back the last
edit, as many times as you need.

00:01:10.245 --> 00:01:13.145
When you are happy, click Done to save the
Layout.

00:01:13.145 --> 00:01:15.175
Cancel leaves it exactly as it was.

00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:19.384
After every edit, the Zones are numbered
again in reading order.

00:01:19.384 --> 00:01:22.231
Those are the numbers the keyboard
shortcuts use.

00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:26.953
A few Layouts people build, depending on
their display.

00:01:27.303 --> 00:01:31.447
On a laptop, two windows is the most that
stays readable: 2 Columns,

00:01:31.447 --> 00:01:33.945
work on the left, reference on the right.

00:01:34.295 --> 00:01:39.079
On an ultrawide display, keep the main
window straight ahead in a wide Zone,

00:01:39.079 --> 00:01:42.163
with narrow Zones at the sides for chat or
music.

00:01:42.513 --> 00:01:47.818
For meetings, a 2 by 2 Grid: the call, its
notes, the shared document and the chat.

00:01:47.818 --> 00:01:50.758
The next lesson shows these Layouts in
action.

00:01:52.308 --> 00:01:57.234
To recap. Edit Layouts, in the menu-bar
menu, opens the Layouts window.

00:01:57.234 --> 00:01:59.870
Edit on your display opens the editor.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:05.490
Click to split, drag a divider to resize,
and Command-click, then Merge, to join.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:07.086
Done saves your Layout.

00:02:08.636 --> 00:02:12.630
In the next lesson, you will see which
Layout fits each way of working,

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:13.699
with real examples.
